# Salesforce Administrator and Access Control

## What is a Salesforce Administrator?

A Salesforce Administrator is responsible for managing and maintaining a Salesforce organization. The administrator ensures that users have the correct access, data is secure, and business processes run smoothly.

### Key Responsibilities
- Managing users and permissions
- Configuring security settings
- Creating and maintaining reports and dashboards
- Customizing objects, fields, and page layouts
- Ensuring data quality and security
- Supporting users and troubleshooting issues

---

# Difference Between User, Role, Profile, and Permission Set

| Feature | User | Role | Profile | Permission Set |
|----------|------|------|----------|---------------|
| Definition | An individual who logs into Salesforce | Determines record visibility in the hierarchy | Defines baseline permissions for a user | Provides additional permissions beyond the profile |
| Purpose | Access Salesforce and perform tasks | Controls data access through role hierarchy | Controls what users can do | Grants extra permissions without changing profiles |
| Assigned To | Individuals | Users | Every user must have one profile | Users as needed |
| Access Control | User-specific | Record-level access | Object, field, and system permissions | Additional object, field, and system permissions |
| Mandatory | Yes | Optional | Yes | Optional |
| Example | Student User | Department Head | Standard User Profile | Report Export Permission |

