# Administrator Access Risks

Providing excessive administrator access can create security risks.

### Risks
1. Unauthorized data access
2. Accidental deletion of records
3. Misconfiguration of security settings
4. Data breaches
5. Compliance violations
6. Abuse of privileged access

### Prevention Measures
- Follow the principle of least privilege
- Grant admin access only when necessary
- Use Permission Sets instead of broad admin rights
- Monitor user activities regularly
- Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
- Conduct periodic security reviews

